35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, the ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, like hall hire. But the bank statements show a third of renewals needed chasing. That’s a lot of work.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, that chasing is exactly the pressure I’m worried about. If people feel hunted for money, they stop coming.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, fixed costs mean everyone pays for empty rooms. But the real issue is who does the chasing. I’ll show you the rota.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the hours confirm it. Chasing individual payments took six hours a month. A yearly collection took one. The burden is real.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, six hours is huge. If the system is too hard, people won’t take the job. We need something simple.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, so a flat fee is easier to manage? But if costs go up, we’re stuck. I need to know if we can afford it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, a flat fee might feel like a tax. If people don’t see the value, they hesitate. I saw that in the turnout.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, hesitation is one thing. But the sign-in sheets show a quarter of people do two-thirds of the work. That’s unfair.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the work is uneven, but the collection is the bottleneck. If we charge per event, the hours skyrocket.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I get it. But if we make it too complicated, new people won’t join. The taster forms say they don’t want a whole year at once.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, that’s a good point. If they don’t want a whole year, maybe a base fee plus event charges is better?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, event charges made weekday turnout drop by a third. People stopped feeling like they belonged. I don’t want that.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, but if we don’t charge for events, the hard workers are subsidizing the ghosts. I want fairness.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, fairness is good, but if the treasurer spends six hours a month chasing money, the club fails. I need a sustainable system.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I agree. But if we’re too strict, we lose the newcomers. The minute books show the old grades caused friction.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,I’m leaning towards a flat fee. It’s the easiest to manage. But I’m worried about the fixed costs.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I’m worried about the flat fee feeling like a burden. I want to protect the quiet members.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I’m voting for whatever spreads the work. But I need to see the options first.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I need a system that minimizes the treasurer’s hours. I’m leaning towards the simplest option.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I want something welcoming. I’m hoping the options give us a choice.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
